WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.926 --> 00:00:17.696
"Ow—drat!" Zann said as he landed in a clawthorn bush.

2
00:00:17.716 --> 00:00:23.441
"That's what you get for zapping in a hurry," Perda said with a laugh.

3
00:00:24.082 --> 00:00:26.103
Zann pushed the prickly branches aside.

4
00:00:26.744 --> 00:00:29.106
He frowned when he saw that Perda wasn't alone.

5
00:00:29.787 --> 00:00:31.228
Darb and Gliss were with her.

6
00:00:32.844 --> 00:00:35.045
"Hi, Zann," Gliss said as Zann climbed out of the bush.

7
00:00:35.065 --> 00:00:37.486
"Need help healing those scratches?"

8
00:00:37.506 --> 00:00:39.407
"No, thanks."

9
00:00:39.927 --> 00:00:41.728
Zann wasn't ready to forgive Gliss yet.

10
00:00:42.388 --> 00:00:47.130
If she hadn't ratted him out to Boz, he might be searching for his parents right now instead

11
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:48.590
of being stuck in Swamp Bottom!

12
00:00:49.391 --> 00:00:50.611
"Um, okay."

13
00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:52.012
Gliss sounded tentative.

14
00:00:52.032 --> 00:00:53.412
"Listen, Zann.

15
00:00:53.612 --> 00:00:54.953
Can we talk for a second?

16
00:00:55.513 --> 00:00:58.534
I really want to—" "Not now," Zann interrupted.

17
00:00:58.554 --> 00:01:00.475
"Perda's note sounded urgent."

18
00:01:01.135 --> 00:01:02.296
He turned toward Perda.

19
00:01:02.576 --> 00:01:03.037
"What's up?"

20
00:01:03.057 --> 00:01:07.140
"I ran into Professor Huli this morning," Perda said.

21
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.662
"I asked her about World X."

22
00:01:10.402 --> 00:01:13.205
Professor Huli was the kids' Advanced Magic teacher.

23
00:01:13.925 --> 00:01:16.888
If anyone might know about World X, it was she.

24
00:01:16.908 --> 00:01:19.310
"Really?" Zann said eagerly.

25
00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:20.651
"What did she say?"

26
00:01:21.591 --> 00:01:22.232
Perda shrugged.

27
00:01:22.252 --> 00:01:23.773
"She's never heard of it."

28
00:01:25.014 --> 00:01:26.115
Zann's heart sank.

29
00:01:26.135 --> 00:01:27.096
"Oh well.

30
00:01:27.964 --> 00:01:32.605
My parents' message made it sound like World X might be a newly discovered world.

31
00:01:33.306 --> 00:01:38.867
So it's no surprise if most people—even an Advanced Magic teacher—haven't heard of it."

32
00:01:38.887 --> 00:01:41.648
"I don't understand," Darb said.

33
00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:44.809
"How is it possible World X was just discovered?

34
00:01:45.509 --> 00:01:47.530
I thought people have been everywhere through the vortex."

35
00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.771
"No, definitely not," Perda said.

36
00:01:50.791 --> 00:01:54.652
"There are probably lots of worlds that haven't been discovered yet.

37
00:01:55.484 --> 00:01:58.206
Most worlds are actually really difficult to find.

38
00:01:58.866 --> 00:02:05.309
There isn't always a direct route from one place to another, and wormholes open and close all the

39
00:02:05.349 --> 00:02:08.851
time, which makes travel through them even more complicated."

40
00:02:09.792 --> 00:02:10.532
Gliss nodded.

41
00:02:10.552 --> 00:02:12.753
"We just learned about all that in school."

42
00:02:12.773 --> 00:02:19.517
"So if Zann's parents got knocked off course by that weird otherworld animal—" Darb glanced at Zann.

43
00:02:19.537 --> 00:02:22.439
"A scatter beast," Zann said.

44
00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:24.900
"They're from a world called Fardark.

45
00:02:25.584 --> 00:02:30.306
My parents mentioned them in one of their books, but nobody knows much about them."

46
00:02:30.966 --> 00:02:34.068
"Zann's parents could be anywhere," Perda continued.

47
00:02:34.088 --> 00:02:37.529
"For all we know, they're in World X right now!"

48
00:02:37.549 --> 00:02:43.651
"Or maybe they're asking around about it while they're looking for a way back to Magica," Zann said.

49
00:02:43.672 --> 00:02:46.193
"It might be a clue, anyway.

50
00:02:46.573 --> 00:02:51.735
If I can get myself back into the vortex—" "That reminds me," Perda interrupted.

51
00:02:51.755 --> 00:02:54.804
"You never told us about your trip with Wyssa.

52
00:02:54.824 --> 00:02:55.704
What was it like?"

53
00:02:56.605 --> 00:03:00.346
"Well, I wasn't in the vortex for long Zann began.

54
00:03:01.226 --> 00:03:03.226
It was hard to describe the experience.

55
00:03:03.326 --> 00:03:04.347
But he did his best.

56
00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:07.688
"Wow. I bet it was cool!"

57
00:03:08.048 --> 00:03:09.028
Perda looked impressed.

58
00:03:09.048 --> 00:03:12.209
"But it sounds like Wyssa did all the work.

59
00:03:12.729 --> 00:03:15.390
Do you think you could navigate through the vortex on your own?"

60
00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.130
Zann shrugged.

61
00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.631
"I'll figure it out."

62
00:03:19.531 --> 00:03:20.811
"What if you don't have enough magic?"

63
00:03:21.171 --> 00:03:22.212
Darb sounded worried.

64
00:03:22.232 --> 00:03:23.592
"You're only a kid."

65
00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.941
"I'm a Red too."

66
00:03:26.742 --> 00:03:29.364
Zann touched his hair, trying to sound confident.

67
00:03:30.265 --> 00:03:32.006
"That should give me some extra power."

68
00:03:32.026 --> 00:03:36.170
"It just sounds too dangerous, Zann," Gliss said.

69
00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:37.991
Zann frowned.

70
00:03:38.011 --> 00:03:41.714
"Everything sounds too dangerous to you," he snapped.

71
00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:45.998
"Especially when it's my parents who are missing instead of yours!"

72
00:03:46.899 --> 00:03:49.261
Gliss gasped, and tears came to her eyes.

73
00:03:49.281 --> 00:03:53.104
"I—I have to go," she mumbled.

74
00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:56.101
Snapping her fingers, she zapped out of sight.

75
00:03:56.121 --> 00:03:58.482
"Zann!" Perda scowled at him.

76
00:03:58.502 --> 00:03:59.883
"That was mean!"

77
00:03:59.903 --> 00:04:02.964
"Gliss was just worried about you," Darb added.

78
00:04:03.804 --> 00:04:04.725
He glanced at Perda.

79
00:04:05.125 --> 00:04:06.285
"Will you take me to check on her?"

80
00:04:06.305 --> 00:04:09.406
"Sure." Perda grabbed Darb's hand.

81
00:04:09.426 --> 00:04:13.748
"Zap!" They disappeared, leaving Zann alone with Zing.

82
00:04:14.549 --> 00:04:16.809
Zann felt guilty for hurting Gliss' feelings.

83
00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.751
But he did his best to shake off his guilt.

84
00:04:20.551 --> 00:04:22.712
In a few days he would be stuck at school.

85
00:04:23.584 --> 00:04:26.887
This could be his last chance to come up with a plan to find his parents.

86
00:04:27.827 --> 00:04:30.729
If his friends didn't want to help, he would do it on his own.

87
00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.872
Two days later Zann was no closer to a plan.

88
00:04:35.773 --> 00:04:41.477
He'd researched the locations of all the known wormholes in Magica, but they were all far away from

89
00:04:41.557 --> 00:04:42.138
Swamp Bottom.

90
00:04:43.198 --> 00:04:49.403
Zapping to any of those wormholes would use up all his energy, leaving little or no energy to

91
00:04:49.463 --> 00:04:50.784
navigate through the vortex.

92
00:04:51.672 --> 00:04:53.973
He would have to rest for at least a day first.

93
00:04:54.753 --> 00:04:59.734
That would give Boz enough time to notice Zann was missing, figure out what was going on, and

94
00:04:59.794 --> 00:05:01.315
stop Zann from leaving Magica.

95
00:05:02.615 --> 00:05:06.996
The day before school was due to start, Zann zapped to the swamp to meet Darb.

96
00:05:07.776 --> 00:05:10.717
Darb had stopped by earlier to set up a time and place to meet.

97
00:05:11.437 --> 00:05:14.418
But when Zann reached their meeting spot, nobody was there.

98
00:05:15.299 --> 00:05:16.099
That was surprising.

99
00:05:16.479 --> 00:05:18.279
Darb was almost always on time.

100
00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:20.220
Zann sat down to wait.

101
00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.562
A moment later Gliss zapped into view.

102
00:05:23.582 --> 00:05:25.683
"Hi, Zann," she said.

103
00:05:26.604 --> 00:05:27.785
Zann jumped to his feet.

104
00:05:28.325 --> 00:05:29.466
"What are you doing here?"

105
00:05:30.787 --> 00:05:34.609
"I asked Darb to arrange to meet you so I could talk to you alone," Gliss said.

106
00:05:34.629 --> 00:05:38.452
"You mean you asked him to help you trick me."

107
00:05:38.932 --> 00:05:39.693
Zann frowned.

108
00:05:39.713 --> 00:05:41.574
"I'm sorry!"

109
00:05:41.914 --> 00:05:42.635
Gliss exclaimed.

110
00:05:42.655 --> 00:05:48.018
"But I've been trying to apologize, and you won't—" Suddenly Perda zapped into view.

111
00:05:48.038 --> 00:05:51.993
"Zann!" she cried, her eyes wide and excited.

112
00:05:52.013 --> 00:05:54.074
"I've been looking for you!

113
00:05:54.774 --> 00:05:56.435
I need to talk to you—now!"

114
00:05:56.455 --> 00:06:03.079
"No problem," said Zann before Perda had a chance to notice Gliss standing behind her.

115
00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.381
Grabbing Perda's hand, he said, "Zap!"

116
00:06:08.562 --> 00:06:10.303
They landed in another part of the swamp.

117
00:06:10.583 --> 00:06:11.624
Perda looked confused.

118
00:06:11.644 --> 00:06:13.905
"Why did you zap us away?"

119
00:06:13.925 --> 00:06:16.286
"Never mind," Zann said.

120
00:06:16.306 --> 00:06:18.167
"What did you want to talk about?"

121
00:06:19.884 --> 00:06:20.706
"Oh!" Perda smiled.

122
00:06:20.726 --> 00:06:25.537
"Right. Listen to this—I just found a new wormhole.

123
00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:28.323
And it's right here in Swamp Bottom!"
